        <body>
            <div xml:id="d271">

                <pb facs="0635" n="597" sameAs="frus:frus1919Parisv11/pg597"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Robert Lansing Papers</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to President Wilson</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-06-28">June 28, 1919</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. President</hi>: It occurs to me that
                    after your departure it will probably be necessary for me on different occasions
                    to refer to conversations which have taken place at the meetings of the Council
                    of Four and as no records of these meetings are at my disposal, I take the
                    liberty of bringing the matter to your attention for such action as you may
                    consider appropriate.</p>
                <p>I believe that Sir Maurice Hankey has the reports of these meetings and at your
                    request will no doubt furnish me with a copy.</p>
                <p>Faithfully yours,</p>
                <closer>[File copy not signed]</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
